# CSS Rules

- Check `src/css/components.css` first for shared classes before adding page-specific overrides.
- Keep page-specific overrides scoped by body/page class (e.g. `.page-about ...`).
- Avoid global selector changes that can impact other pages unintentionally.
- For hero/image fixes: confirm interactions between position/height/object-fit/object-position.
- Prefer minimal, targeted overrides over large rewrites.
- Keep typography, spacing, and color tokens consistent with existing variables/usages.
- If changing nav or hero behavior, verify impact on homepage, about, and story pages.
